{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ef7e39d99b57bc5af2", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Alternating Current - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890667b"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906636", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065cf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b58"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :<br /><strong>Statement-I:</strong> The reactance of an ac circuit is zero. It is possible that the circuit contains a capacitor and an inductor.<br /><strong>Statement-II:</strong> In ac circuit, the average power delivered by the source never becomes zero.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below"}, "options": [{"id": "f8d5c1", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d0"}, {"id": "42216b", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d1"}, {"id": "870bbe", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d2"}, {"id": "8e9a85", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "<p>The angular frequency of alternating current in a L-C-R circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The components connected are shown in the figure. Find the value of inductance of the coil and capacity of condenser.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff5afaa00-7567-4dca-be66-c710a45ece32-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 384px; height: 199px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d10052", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d5"}, {"id": "a6988c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d6"}, {"id": "76472f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d7"}, {"id": "c94d0d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065d9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "A transformer has an efficiency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and works at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kW</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the secondary voltage is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the current in the secondary coil is:"}, "options": [{"id": "812d80", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>59</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065da"}, {"id": "26fda5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065db"}, {"id": "7f4330", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065dc"}, {"id": "62e6d2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065dd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065de", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5b"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa022"], "question": {"text": "In a series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></math> circuit with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>,&nbsp;power factor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. If a capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math> is added to the circuit the power factor becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "426d3f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065df"}, {"id": "ba8548", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e0"}, {"id": "f5bc80", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e1"}, {"id": "d2b3cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An alternating voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>220</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> volt is applied to a purely resistive load of <math><mn>50</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . The time taken for the current to rise from half of the peak value to the peak value is:"}, "options": [{"id": "339aaa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>7.21</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e4"}, {"id": "6f54d1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e5"}, {"id": "08905b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2.24</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e6"}, {"id": "17df19", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3.33</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4712"], "question": {"text": "A series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;circuit is connected to a battery of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>. If the circuit is switched on at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the time at which the energy stored in the inductor reaches&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math> times of its maximum value, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "166632", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065e9"}, {"id": "206e0e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ea"}, {"id": "325ab0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065eb"}, {"id": "acbdb1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ed", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the given circuit, comment on the type of transformer used :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8e141329-2808-43de-9e37-05c76f8b3330-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 161px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d2e15d", "text": "Auxilliary transformer", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ee"}, {"id": "1fd02c", "text": "Auto transformer", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ef"}, {"id": "6333b8", "text": "Step-up transformer", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f0"}, {"id": "f18be4", "text": "Step down transformer", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5b"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa022"], "question": {"text": "A series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></math> circuit connected with an ac source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo> </mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>1000</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> has a power factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>. If the source of emf is changed to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, the new power factor of the circuit will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "fc8e11", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f3"}, {"id": "2d49c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f4"}, {"id": "34a79b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f5"}, {"id": "0570f7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I : An AC circuit undergoes electrical resonance if it contains either a capacitor or an inductor.</p><p>Statement II: An AC circuit containing a pure capacitor or a pure inductor consumes high power due to its non-zero power factor. In the light of above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7c82c1", "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f8"}, {"id": "0f27b3", "text": "Statement I is true but statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065f9"}, {"id": "f7a4fc", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065fa"}, {"id": "6bf9c6", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065fc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["6162fb3c6ed13040ec84c90b"], "question": {"text": "The equation of current in a purely inductive circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the inductance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>mH</mi></math> then the equation for the voltage across the inductor, will be"}, "options": [{"id": "cbbc15", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065fd"}, {"id": "49f095", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065fe"}, {"id": "228520", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a89065ff"}, {"id": "a0de7a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906600"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906601", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "A transformer consisting of <math><mn>300</mn></math> turns in the 