he circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When capacitor with capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math> is put in series, the power factor becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "4c99cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906607"}, {"id": "23ca27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906608"}, {"id": "ef9efe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906609"}, {"id": "32f76d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e94a2493707322b06e318f"], "question": {"text": "Two identical capacitors <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> charged to the same potential <math><mn>5</mn><mi>V</mi></math> are connected in two different circuits as shown below at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the charge on capacitors <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></math> respectively, then (Here <math><mi>e</mi></math> is the base of natural logarithm)<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F87177991-a74d-479d-8bcb-e0ca05b76539-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 170px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "8726ce", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660c"}, {"id": "aea3a4", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660d"}, {"id": "523b08", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660e"}, {"id": "b501a8", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890660f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906610", "ty