>o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906611"}, {"id": "ca4dfb", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906612"}, {"id": "2416ff", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906613"}, {"id": "192420", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>150</mn><mi>o</mi></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906614"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906615", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "<p>Primary coil of a transformer is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. Primary and secondary turns of the transforms are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> respectively. Secondary coil of transformer is connected to two series resistances as shown in figure. The output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">0</mn></msub></mfenced></math> is :</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F77e61619-9ac8-4ca3-915e-7e2c83f345b6.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 144px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "ddf688", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906616"}, {"id": "b86c46", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906617"}, {"id": "1115de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906618"}, {"id": "375864", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906619"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5b"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa022"], "question": {"text": "In a series LCR circuit, the inductive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and the capacitive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The power factor of the circuit is :"}, "options": [{"id": "4b3deb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661b"}, {"id": "3ff256", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661c"}, {"id": "bd6c9d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661d"}, {"id": "131af5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890661f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b58"], "question": {"text": "An electric bulb rated as $100 \\mathrm{~W}-220 \\mathrm{~V}$ is connected to an ac source of rms voltage 220 V. The peak value of current through the bulb is :"}, "options": [{"id": "188aaf", "text": "$0.64\\mathrm{~A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906620"}, {"id": "fd4f72", "text": "$0.45\\mathrm{~A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906621"}, {"id": "282e31", "text": "$2.2\\mathrm{~A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906622"}, {"id": "6b3087", "text": "$0.32\\mathrm{~A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906623"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906624", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "A series LCR circuit is connected to an alternating source of emf E. The current amplitude at resonant frequency is $I_0$. If the value of resistance R becomes twice of its initial value then amplitude of current at resonance will be"}, "options": [{"id": "ab78ed", "text": "$2 \\mathrm{I}_0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906625"}, {"id": "87dd21", "text": "$I_0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906626"}, {"id": "6344ec", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906627"}, {"id": "e67d81", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{\\sqrt{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906628"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906629", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "<p>Magnetic materials used for making permanent magnets&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and magnets in a transformer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;have different properties of the following, which property best matches for the type of magnet required?</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "497e96", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;Large retentivity, small coercivity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662a"}, {"id": "40c39e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;small&nbsp; retentivity, large coercivity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662b"}, {"id": "05c6ef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;Large retentivity, large&nbsp;coercivity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662c"}, {"id": "e1a81b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;large retentivity, large coercivity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An ac current is represented as<br/>$\\mathrm{i}=5 \\sqrt{2}+10 \\cos \\left(650 \\pi \\mathrm{t}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\mathrm{Amp}$<br/>The r.m.s value of the current is"}, "options": [{"id": "980c87", "text": "50 Amp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890662f"}, {"id": "8b124b", "text": "100 Amp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906630"}, {"id": "9c2883", "text": "10 Amp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906631"}, {"id": "d52b9a", "text": "$5 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{Amp}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906632"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:29.745Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:29.745Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906679"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906677", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890665b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "A alternating current at any instant is given by $i=[6+\\sqrt{56} \\sin (100 \\pi t+\\pi / 3)]$ A. The $r m s$ value of the current is ________ A."}, "options": [{"id": "2c895f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890665c"}, {"id": "4a259b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890665d"}, {"id": "ba21c9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890665e"}, {"id": "c0ef15", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890665f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906660", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the given circuit the current through battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> just after closing the switch &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&#39; will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fced56931-7874-4880-93a5-58c911c1bb12-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 229px; height: 150px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a48080", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906661"}, {"id": "07ff27", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906662"}, {"id": "ed0e5b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906663"}, {"id": "96fcb4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906664"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906665", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "A common transistor radio set requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> for its operation. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> source is constructed by using a transformer and a rectifier circuit, which are operated at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> on standard domestic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> supply. The number of turns of secondary coil are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the number of turns of primary are"}, "options": [{"id": "5e1802", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906666"}, {"id": "e370b8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906667"}, {"id": "fa2de1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906668"}, {"id": "73edb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a8906669"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0dc677dc36a890666a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5b"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa022"], "question": {"text": "A series LCR circuit is connected to an AC source of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The circuit contains a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>, an inductor of inductive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>, and a capacitor of capacitive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>130</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The power factor of circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=